#N canvas 20 20 1400 800 12;
#X text 20 20 panic-poke -- fires panic every 25 seconds so the recovery can be tested by hand. Load it as a THIRD patch after mother.pd and main.pd. NOTHING ON THE DEVICE SENDS panic: it has consumers -- u_init's safe exit and u_tempo -- but the only writers are the bench and the Mac dev panel. This exists so you do not have to sit through a fifteen-step bench run to see one thing., f 96;
#X text 20 130 WHAT TO WATCH. On panic the aux button goes RED and the footer says panic. THEN PRESS AUX: the button must go GREEN and the footer must go back to the BPM. A footer still reading panic after the transport has visibly restarted is the bug this patch was written for -- it was real \, and it was found by doing exactly this on the device., f 96;
#X obj 20 300 loadbang;
#X obj 20 345 del 5000;
#X obj 300 390 metro 25000;
#X obj 20 470 t b b;
#X msg 20 520 bang;
#X obj 20 570 s panic;
#X msg 480 660 PANIC SENT -- expect RED and a panic footer -- now press aux and the footer must return to the BPM;
#X obj 480 730 print;
#X obj 700 300 r disp;
#X obj 700 345 route status led;
#X obj 700 400 print FOOTER;
#X obj 900 400 print LED;
#X text 700 470 The two prints are the same thing the OLED is being told \, so the console and the screen can be compared directly. FOOTER should read panic and then the BPM again \; LED should read panic and then running., f 60;
#X connect 2 0 3 0;
#X connect 3 0 4 0;
#X connect 3 0 5 0;
#X connect 4 0 5 0;
#X connect 5 1 8 0;
#X connect 5 0 6 0;
#X connect 6 0 7 0;
#X connect 8 0 9 0;
#X connect 10 0 11 0;
#X connect 11 0 12 0;
#X connect 11 1 13 0;
